  "worked_solution": "First, we find the limit of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to \\,-1}f(t) & =({lim}_{t\\to \\,-1}{t}^{3})i+({lim}_{t\\to \\,-1}{t}^{2})j+({lim}_{t\\to \\,-1}\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(t+2))k \\\\  & =(-1)^{3}\\,i+(-1)^{2}\\,j+\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(-1+2)\\,k \\\\  & =-i+j \\\\ {lim}_{t\\to \\,-1}g(t) & =({lim}_{t\\to \\,-1}\\frac{2}{t})i+({lim}_{t\\to \\,-1}(3-t))j-({lim}_{t\\to \\,-1}({t}^{2}-1))k \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{(-1)}\\,i+(3-(-1))\\,j-((-1)^{2}-1)k \\\\  & =-2\\,i+4\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use properties of limits to calculate the final result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to \\,-1}[4f(t)-7g(t)] & ={lim}_{t\\to \\,-1}4f(t)-{lim}_{t\\to \\,-1}7g(t) \\\\  & =4{lim}_{t\\to \\,-1}f(t)-7{lim}_{t\\to \\,-1}g(t) \\\\  & =4(-i+j)-7(-2\\,i+4\\,j) \\\\  & =-4\\,i+4\\,j+14\\,i-28\\,j \\\\  & =10\\,i-24\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$",
